al with  the size of that apk right without  having abilities to prune down the size  of the model and you would have to build  your own framework for loading that  machine learning model into the device  itself so the reality is what you would  probably end up doing is hosting a  prediction service in the cloud on your  servers and having that molded with  mobile device call out to that endpoint  with  arrest API and doing that you incur all  the kind of detractions that we kind of  talked about earlier wherein you can't  have these immersive experiences where  you can't point a camera at something  and instantly have it show what it is  so tensorflow has really changed scheme  there and what's really great is that  not only does it work for what i've  shown you today with android but it is  also equivalent on iOS and raspberry pi  so you can deploy your mobile app across  all their favorite platforms another  reason that tensorflow has been  fantastic both for me and for all of you  is the community so many people are  making examples with tensorflow creating  really cool use cases answering each  other's questions and supporting and  helping each other grow and build great  experiences and that's only in the most  recent year and change and now that  tensorflow is 1.0 as of mid-february  you can use it with confidence in  production knowing that the API will not  change under you until potential flow  2.0 which is so far down the road that I  haven't even give another thought until  just now so machine learning on mobile  leads to awesome experiences you can do  it now without having to you utilize the  the pains of the past and tooling has  gone to a point where you can  essentially follow a recipe and have it  work and moreover to be able to do it  for your specific application is what  makes it really powerful because you  could certainly load up inception that  network with its pre training system  that can recognize a thousand different  things but they're just kind of random  things boats and oranges and trees and  houses and streets and sidewalks  you care about specific things right you  want to build an app that can recognize  your things so being able to retrain it  and being able to retrain it with ease  with captioning video without having to  amass terabytes of data and spend weeks  of time to load process and train up a  model and then still have to make two  consideration about mobile makes this  quite awesome and so feel free to come  up at the end we can play with the the  app that I made but that's really a toy  example you saw the way I was capturing  that video I was just kind of walking  around taking the video trying to do it  on a white background because I knew the  podium would be white but in your real  case example real-world example you  would perhaps do it with a variety of  backgrounds maybe in shade and in  sunlight  maybe on white surfaces on carpet on  wood on metal think about where your  users might see the things that you want  to recognize so that's kind of the whole  process as a training pipeline and it  allows you to think of it as something  that you don't have to have a huge  burden on anymore you can basically pour  the data in at the top and then have  machine learning in an app coming out  the other side it's no longer a problem  where you say well let's see if we're  going to make this work we might need to  hire a team of PhDs to think about how  we can recognize our specific product  they're very subtle some of them are  only a little bit different from the  others inception can take care of that  the model itself notices the most minut  differences and hopefully many if not  all of you have had a chance to wander a  little bit about around the third floor  is that during the conference where we  have the example with the candy sorter  which is based on a Japanese farmer who  built basically this system  but on a Raspberry Pi to sort his  cucumbers and I don't know about you but  I can't tell the difference between  cucumbers they all kind of look the same  even at the store there's like normal  cucumbers and then they have the fancy  ones that are called like European  cucumbers and there's like longer and  thin but they're all packaged in plastic  so I never know whether or not they're  more fresh or less fresh and in Japan  there's tons of different types of  cucumbers and this guy's growing them  all together and before he had to  categorize these all himself because you  sell them to different places right and  now he has a system that does it for him  and in that situation you have a very  controlled environment he knows the  cucumbers will come down this conveyer  belt he's got the camera and he will see  it in this orientation in my situation I  knew that I would be pointing my camera  at the podium at an angle with a white  background under bright lights so when I  trained my model I found a white table  with bright lights and pointed my camera  in my video at my objects I walked  around in a circle to cover the angles  but I didn't do much else because I  didn't need to so you can solve kind of  a whole range of problems depending on  your particular use case and so thinking  through this problem in in this model in  this mode where and you don't  necessarily have to completely start  from scratch but just thinking about a  few key points can help with the design  consideration so to speak and save a lot  of trouble down the road  and so I mentioned that there is a way  to retrain this or do this online right  because the conferences add a closed and  so I have a short link for you there you  can do this online that will guide you  through the process of retraining the  network so then you just have something  on your computer that does this and for  the mobile side of things if you go over  to tensorflow org slash  mobile it will point you to the Android  the iOS and the Raspberry Pi github  examples that you can literally clone  build and employ straight up  no code changes and then once you have  that working you can connect the two  together you can take the transfer  learning that inception that first code  lab take the output of that run the  graph transform tool and then replace  the graph that was in your Android  assets folder with that one and then  finally it has the cloud machine  learning resource there to learn more  about that and how to get at that part  working though the code that's the top  does talk about that so with that I want  to thank you guys  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

